WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
A context window is the amount of text, instructions, conversation history,

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.445
retrieved content, examples, and tool output a model can consider during a request.

00:00:08.445 --> 00:00:12.240
It is the working space the model has available when producing an answer.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:15.510
Everything placed into that space competes for attention: system instructions,

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:20.000
developer instructions, user requests, prior messages, documents, summaries, code,

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:23.175
citations, and the output the model is expected to generate.

00:00:23.175 --> 00:00:25.445
Context is measured in tokens, not words.

00:00:25.445 --> 00:00:29.080
A token can be a whole word, part of a word, punctuation, spacing,

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:31.475
or another text fragment depending on the tokenizer.

00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:35.420
The exact conversion varies, but the engineering point is simple: every instruction,

00:00:35.420 --> 00:00:39.000
document, example, and response consumes part of a finite budget.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.110
Output tokens matter too,

00:00:40.110 --> 00:00:44.510
because a request that fills the entire input space may leave too little room for a useful

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:44.975
answer.

00:00:44.975 --> 00:00:48.995
Large context windows change workflows because they let teams include more source material

00:00:48.995 --> 00:00:50.500
before asking for analysis.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:53.650
A model can review longer documents, more code, richer chat history,

00:00:53.650 --> 00:00:55.500
or larger sets of retrieved evidence.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:59.290
That does not mean the model understands everything equally well or that structure stops

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:00.000
mattering.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:03.070
More room helps only when the information is relevant, organized,

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.690
and clearly tied to the task.

00:01:04.690 --> 00:01:06.940
Context management is an engineering discipline.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:10.500
It involves deciding what to include, what to summarize, how to order material,

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:12.820
how to label sources, how to preserve provenance,

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.495
and how to prevent noise from burying important facts.

00:01:15.495 --> 00:01:17.000
The goal is not to fill the window.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:20.720
The goal is to give the model the right information in a form it can use effectively.
